% Bridges: the words of a listing, in the words of the tariff.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a value* is a word for the construction *a construction*.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.

the knowledge base garments background includes:

"tee shirt" is a word for the kind T-shirt.
"t-shirt" is a word for the kind T-shirt.
"shirt" is a word for the kind shirt.
"knit" is a word for the construction knitted.
"woven" is a word for the construction woven.

the marketplace fields is published at "https://example.org/marketplace/fields".

rule kind_by_name with provenance the marketplace fields:
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind the kind.

rule construction_by_field with provenance the marketplace fields:
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the field "craft of weaving" of the garment reads a value
    and the value is a word for the construction the construction.

scenario tee is:
    item one is called "tee shirt".
    the field "craft of weaving" of item one reads "knit".
    kinds expects answers ["the kind of item one is T-shirt"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of item one is knitted"].

query kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.
